1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,770
Ten minutes of AI...

2
00:00:01,980 --> 00:00:04,720
and people gave up almost twice as often.

3
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:07,760
Picture your AI chatbot as training wheels.

4
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:10,070
Over a thousand people did math.

5
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:12,240
About half got the wheels.

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,920
Then, without warning...

7
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:15,570
the wheels came off.

8
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:19,590
Alone, they solved fewer problems than people who never had them.

9
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:22,250
And they hit skip almost twice as often.

10
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:23,420
Reading, too.

11
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:26,040
No AI: 1 skip in 100.

12
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,890
After AI: 8.

13
00:00:27,890 --> 00:00:31,630
Researchers think AI trains us to expect instant answers...

14
00:00:31,630 --> 00:00:33,580
so we never learn to balance.

15
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:34,840
Here's the weird part.

16
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,770
People who only asked for hints...

17
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:39,340
did about as well as people with no AI.

18
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:40,230
The catch?

19
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:41,340
Short tests.

20
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:43,990
And the hint finding is a clue, not proof.

21
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:46,240
So ask your AI for a hint first...

22
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:47,270
not the answer.

23
00:00:47,270 --> 00:00:49,770
Like a hand on the bike seat... that lets go.

24
00:00:49,770 --> 00:00:52,880
There's one word in this video I never said out loud.

25
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,660
Spotted it?

26
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:54,440
Comment it.

27
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:57,150
Follow for more AI, explained like this.

28
00:00:57,150 --> 00:00:58,060
And remember...

29
00:00:58,060 --> 00:00:59,560
all it took was...
